[ti:Day 17]

[00:00.00]aspect 例 It is an important aspect of China's trade policy to respect the local custom of the buying country. 尊重买方国家的风俗习惯是中国 贸易政策的一个重要方面。
[00:14.40]consult 例 The committee does not adequately consult others when drafting amendments. 委员会在起 草修正案时没有充分征求他人的意见。
[00:26.08]nominal 例 The managing director has the nominal power; however, the company is run by his wife. 总经理名义上掌权，但实际管理公司的是他 的妻子。
[00:38.72]hack 例 The financial budget has been hacked almost in half. 财政预算几乎被削减了一半。
[00:46.56]forward 例 Please forward all the letters to me while I'm on holiday. 我外出度假期间请把给我的信件 都转寄给我。
[00:55.52]admissible 例 It is not admissible that the staff in our company dress in casual clothing during office hours. 我们公司不允许员工在上班期间穿便服。
[01:10.08]tailor 例 The firm can tailor a large order to individual requirements. 对于大额订单，该公司 可以按个性化需求进行生产。
[01:19.52]certify 例 Securities laws currently require research analysts to personally certify that their reports accurately reflect their views of a stock. 现行 证券法要求研究分析师亲自证明报告准确反映了 他们对某只股票的看法。
[01:39.52]abstain 例 His decision to abstain from voting faced strong opposition. 他放弃投票的决定遭到了强烈
[01:49.12]indispensable 例 One of the indispensable functions of an organisation is to promote communication among individuals. 一个组织必不可少的职能之 一是促进个体间的沟通。
[02:05.28]filibuster 例 Harry Reid, the majority leader in the Senate, needs 60 votes to break a filibuster. 参议院多数党领袖哈里•里德需要60票才能挫败阻 碍议案通过的行动。
[02:18.25]existence 例 The company has gone bankrupt after being an existence for three years. 该公司在运 营三年后宣告破产。
[02:29.45]criterion 例 Establishing criterion for investment of a nation's resources is crucially important for poor countries. 对穷国来说，建立国家资源的投 资标准是至关重要的。
[02:45.61]consideration 例 Objections to the plan will be taken into consideration. 对本计划的异议将予以考虑。
[02:55.53]reinvest 例 He sold his shares and then reinvested the proceeds into other assets. 他卖掉自己的股 份，然后将收益再投资到其他资产中去。
[03:06.41]centralise 例 The company has built a new headquarters in London to centralise its administration. 为了 能够集中管理，公司在伦敦新建了总部。
[03:19.69]nullify 例 That negative attitude will nullify all the efforts of hunting for a job. 消极的态度会使求 职所付出的努力都付诸东流。
[03:30.73]emerge 例 A smile emerged on her face on hearing that she had a promotion. 当听到升职的消息 时，她脸上露出了笑容。
[03:40.17]floppy 例 Sony ceased all floppy disk production due to the lack of demand in 2011. 在2011年，由于 产品需求量极低，索尼公司停止了软盘的生产。
[03:50.89]endeavour 例 The company endeavours to give the best service you could ever imagine. 该公司致力于 为您提供最好的服务。
[04:02.09]promote 例 The unique design of the packing will help us promote the sale of mobiles. 外包装的独特 设计将有助于我们销售这些手机。
[04:13.14]federation 例 According to the federation rules, all sponsors must remain anonymous for their own protection. 根据联合会的规章，为保护资助 人自身的利益，所有资助人必须匿名。
[04:28.02]intangible 例 We should try to quantify and measure these seemingly intangible elements. 我们应试 着量化和衡量这些看似无形的元素。
[04:40.02]prioritise 例 It was a hard-won opportunity but he had to prioritise his health. 尽管这是一个难得的机 会，但他必须把健康放在首位。
[04:50.58]backbone 例 Now the company has $500 million in annual sales and 4,000 employees and is building much of this country's Internet backbone. 目前该公司的年销售额已高达5亿美 元，拥有4000名雇员，并且在该国因特网的发展 中成为骨干力量。
[05:08.98]estimate 例 They estimate that last year computers sold online were 12% cheaper than in stores. 他们估计，去年网上销售的电脑比实体店便宜 12%。
[05:21.62]absenteeism 例 Finally he was dismissed from his post because of his absenteeism. 由于旷工，他最终 被解雇了。
[05:32.50]flashy 例 Rather than relying on distracting flashy ads, we developed relevant, clearly marked textbased ads to the right of our search results. 我们不发布华而不实的广告，而是把一些 有关联度的、简单明了的文本广告放在搜索结果 的右侧。
[05:51.86]customise 例 He has had his own car customised by request of his daughter. 应女儿的要求，他已经 请人改装了自己的汽车。
[06:01.46]remedy 例 The company gave him a remedy for negligent damage to property. 该公司因过失损 害财产对他进行赔偿。
[06:11.06]ream 例 He wrote reams on the topic. 围绕这个话 题，他写了很多。 scrap value 废料价值
[06:15.54]cumulative 例 The WHO will adjust the figures in its cumulative cases following the results of this external verification. 在获得这一外部核实的结果 之后，世界卫生组织将调整其累计病例的数字。
[06:32.03]highlight 例 I can highlight that by investigating the nature of the workload. 我可以通过调查工作量 的性质来突出那一点。 morning session 上午市；前市
[06:42.43]footnote 例 Book reading strengthened our analytical skills, encouraging us to pursue an observation all the way down to the footnote. 读书增强了我们的分析能力，鼓励我们针对书的 内容，甚至每个注解，去发表自己的看法。
[07:00.51]decentralise 例 Decentralising is a part of the adjustment of the government power structure. 职权下放 是政府权力结构调整的一部分。
[07:13.15]markup 例 The markup on housing prices this month is about 10 percent. 这个月房价的涨幅大概有 10%。
[07:22.27]illustrious 例 Steve Jobs is no doubt one of the most illustrious CEOs. 史蒂夫•乔布斯无疑是最杰出的 CEO之一。
[07:31.55]contrast 例 This sympathy is perceived to contrast with the harsh treatment of carmakers. 人们注意 到，这种同情与汽车制造商受到的苛刻待遇形成 对照。
[07:43.55]assay 例 The ore assays 75 percent of gold. 这种矿 石经验定含金量为75%。
[07:48.99]concrete 例 Various concrete measures were enumerated in the plan. 计划中列举了各种具体 办法。
[07:57.95]fancy 例 Dress at the party was informal, with no neckties or fancy dress. 人们参加聚会时穿衣很 随意，既不打领带也不穿高档的礼服。
[08:07.55]beckon 例 It is impolite to use a finger to beckon someone. 用一个手指示意别人过来是不礼貌的。
[08:15.07]inflammable 例 These materials are highly inflammable. 这 些材料都高度易燃。
[08:22.59]vital 例 It is vital for us to get financial support as soon as possible. 对我们来说，尽快得到经济援 助至关重要。
[08:31.87]conform 例 These plans are in the best interest of the enterprise and also conform to laws and regulations. 这些计划是出于企业利益最大化考 虑，并且符合法律及规章制度。
